WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.760
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.343
SPEAKER: What's the
difference between

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:06.040
a globally-distributed database
with strong consistency and one

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:06.920
without?

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.470
Predictability.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.290
No missing data, no
out-of-sync data,

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.720
reliable accuracy every time.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.540
With Google Cloud Spanner,
the horizontally-scalable

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.710
relational database, your data
is available when it's needed.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.860
And it's consistent no
matter where your users are.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.160
It's a predictability
that you can depend on.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.730
With other databases offering
less-than-strong consistency,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.770
your data may or
may not be there

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.920
when your users need
it most, or even worse,

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.630
it may not be accurate.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.180
Google Cloud Spanner gives
you all of the benefits

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.950
of a relational database--

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.740
simplicity, speed,
and data integrity--

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.320
while scaling to handle
even the most challenging

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.550
of transactional workloads.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.900
Google Cloud Spanner.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.490
Never choose between scale
and data accuracy again.

